WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 line:92%
-Our next guest represents

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.869
New Jersey's 3rd district in
the House of Representatives

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Congressman Andy Kim.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks for being here,
Congressman.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks, Seth,
for having me on your show

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:13.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, this is a historic
and somber day.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want
to talk about that, as well.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.617
But I also want to talk abou
the events of January 6th.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:20.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think a lot of peopl
became aware of you

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of these photos of you
sort of helping clean up

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
during the aftermath
of the riots

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
that happened
in the Capitol building.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:35.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
What led you to sort of
make the decision to do this

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember I was walking
through the Capitol

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the very first time
after the siege had ended,

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:44.511
the insurrection had ended
and I got to the Rotunda.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:47.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is such
a beautiful room, Seth.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's -- You know,
I think the Capitol building

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the most beautiful building
in the country,

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the Rotunda
is the center of --

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.890
the building is the center o
our democracy in many ways

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.827 line:92%
And it was disgraced that day.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:04.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
People had defiled the room,
the building.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.566
You know, I saw trash and
garbage all over the place

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:09.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw cigarette butts put ou
on statues in the Rotunda

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.304 line:92%
and thrown on this ground.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was --
It was really tough.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:16.609 line:92%
And so when you love something

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's broken,
you want to fix it.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.679 line:92%
And I tried to do what I could

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be able
to just get it in better shape

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:24.150
I didn't want to see
the sun to rise the next morning

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
on a broken Congress,
so I picked up a trash bag

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just started
cleaning up the Capitol.

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:32.192
-When did you become aware
of the fact that this had become

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:35.462
sort of a viral phenomenon
these photos of you cleaning up?

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:39.799
-Yeah. You know, it was no
something I was expecting.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:44.471
And I remember, the next
morning, my wife called me

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:47.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said that she was
on a video confe--

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
a video meeting for her work
and one of her co-workers

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.178 line:92%
sent it to her, this photo

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
that her aunt
sent to this co-worker.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
So my wife called me,
told me about it.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said that when she saw it,
she immediately was like,

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:02.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That's so Andy. That's exactl
what he would do."

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:04.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then she said
she just started to cry

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:07.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I think just --
it was a lot for her to proces

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
of what me and my colleagues
and others went through

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
and our country went through
that day.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:15.034
And I think that the picture has
really -- it touched her heart

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
It touched
a lot of people's hearts.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:19.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I think it just
represents that kind of --

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
that decency,
that small act of kindness

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:27.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
that kind of service mind-se

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:30.617
that I think many people
are yearning for right now

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:34.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did it ever strike you that
not just you, obviously,

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:38.658
but anyone who was cleaning up
was cleaning up a crime scene,

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:42.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that, to some degree,
moving evidence

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:43.429 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that could be used?

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
As we know now there
are multiple investigation

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.401 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
opened by the FBI.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was actually
the first thought

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:50.837 line:92%
that went through my mind.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.573
And, in fact, there were som
officers there in the room

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:57.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I immediately went to them,
and I just said,

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:00.780
"Do you need this stuff?
Do you need anything here?

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.081 line:92%
And, you know, they said no.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:05.919
They said, "It's just here
It's gonna be cleaned up."

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:08.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, you know,
I started cleaning it up.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were water bottles,
personal clothing,

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.925 line:92%
but there was some stuff.

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:12.926 line:92%
I came across body armor.

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.194 line:92%
There was literally body armor

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
there on the floor
in the Rotunda.

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:17.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went to them
with this, I said,

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Is this yours,
or is this someone else's?

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:22.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said,
"No, it must've been someone

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.237 size:78% position:39% line:92%
in the insurrection."

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:26.639
So we went through that.
There was a serial number.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
We found out
that this body armor

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
was actually just purchase
two weeks ago.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.478
This was not something that yo
can just get over the counter.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:36.916
It's tactical-grade, and it wa
just purchased two weeks ago

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:40.019
so someone purchased this
for the express purposes

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:43.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
of wearing it to January 6th
to the Capitol building.

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:46.526
That's really frightening
when you think about it.

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously,
that day was terrifying.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:51.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm wondering how frightenin
it is now

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.333 line:92%
to return to your workplace.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:57.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
And obviously,
security has been beefed u

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
since the day
of the insurrection.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
National Guard
has been called in.

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:01.708 line:92%
I believe this is a photo

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.509 size:84% position:42%
from either last night
or a couple nights ago.

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:06.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is you visiting the
National Guard from New Jersey

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:09.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
your home state,
and bringing them some coffee.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.850 line:92%
Was the coffee appreciated

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.019 line:92%
And how are they feeling about

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
being brought
into the nation's Capitol?

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
The coffee was appreciated

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
They set off a little bit
of a debate on whether or no

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should've brought
Wawa coffee from Jersey,

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.464 size:84% position:42% line:92%
but it was appreciated.

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, look, what the Capito
looks like right now,

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.303 line:92%
it's a fortress right now.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:36.276
And I walked through the halls
of the Capitol, and it was -

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:38.444
I have to tell you, I've never
seen anything like it, Seth.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:41.414
It was surreal was perhaps
the only word I can use.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:45.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw thousands
of servicemembers, uniformed

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:47.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
strewn out
all throughout the hallways.

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.222 line:92%
I mean, we have right now

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:54.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
United States soldiers
and servicemembers,

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:58.298
you know, we have guardsme
quartered in our Capitol.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is the first time
since the Civil War

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
since we've had
anything like this.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.237 line:92%
And, you know, it just shows you

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:07.940 size:84% position:42%
just how unprecedented
of a situation this is.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
What we also --
I got briefed on the threats

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.411 size:75% position:38%
against the Capitol,
and they were real.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are real and present
threats against us.

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.915
And I used to work in national
security in counterterrorism

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.418
and the kind of briefing I got
about the threats on the Capitol

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:22.055
were more akin to the briefing
I got when I was in Afghanistan.

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this is scary.
And, you know,

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:27.126 size:84% position:42%
we have an inauguration
just in a couple days,

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:31.898
and I'm really worried about
what's about to happen next.

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, you talk about
unprecedented.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:36.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, we have now for
the first time in our history,

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:39.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
a president
who's been impeached twice

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, again,
there's so much going on.

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:45.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one, I think,
position that those

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.448
on the other side of the aisle
would say as a criticism is,

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:51.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How can you both impeach
one President

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:54.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
while also launching
with the Joe Biden presidency?

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:56.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think it's possible
for Congress

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:58.658 line:92%
to do both at the same time?

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We have to do both
at the same time.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.129
And this is something that
I've been very insistent on.

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:05.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have to make sure
we move forward,

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:07.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's also
incredibly important

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we don't minimize
what happened on January 6th

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:14.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
What happened on January 6th
was literally an attack

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:17.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
from one branch of governmen
against another.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:19.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that
that is something that reall

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:21.414 line:92%
has to sink in for all of us

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:24.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if we were to just think
about this as,

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:26.552 size:88% position:44%
"Oh, well, we can't push
this forward right now

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
in terms of accountability
on the President

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.690 size:84% position:42%
because of the incoming
Biden administration.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.825
He's got appointees that
he needs to get confirmed

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:34.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
and legislation
that we need to do,"

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:39.165
then we are just minimizin
what happened on January 6th

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:41.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
as if it was just
any other policy issue,

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:45.671
as if it was just, you know,
another vote on the docket

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:46.606 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it's not.

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:50.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need to make sure
that we treat this as the --

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:54.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
just the absolute disaster
that it was

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
and one of the most dark day
in our democracy.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:00.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it cannot be normalize
or minimized,

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:03.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we'd be doing our countr
a disservice if we did.

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:07.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, it's sadly too easy
to forget about

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
the mounting death tolls
of COVID

00:07:10.363 --> 00:07:12.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
as it's sort of pushed off
the front pages

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:15.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the events
that happened last week.

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:19.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some of your colleagues
were in a room, a closed room,

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:22.275
with Republican colleagues
who wouldn't wear masks.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:24.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
We now have three Democratic
Congressmen --

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.478 line:92%
Congresspeople -- excuse me --

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:28.581 size:81% position:41%
who've tested positive
for COVID since that.

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:30.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
we have a lot of Republicans

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:32.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
calling for unity today
as their defense

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:35.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
for why we shouldn't impeach
the President.

00:07:35.021 --> 00:07:36.756
What's it like knowing
that they won't even take

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:39.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
basic safety precautions
in a time like that?

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:42.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
In a time where, look, I think
Republican Congressmen --

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:45.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congresspeople had exactly
as much to be scared of

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
during that day,
and yet in a closed room,

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.502 line:92%
they wouldn't put masks on

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:52.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely. I remember
I returned to the House floo

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:54.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
after the insurrection
had been quelled,

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:57.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I sat there
just right on the aisle --

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:59.812
on the other side of the aisle
from the Republican colleagues

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:03.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was just thinking ther
at that moment, like,

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:05.751 line:92%
"Is anything going to change

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:08.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
Perhaps are they
going to find the errors

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:11.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
of what they were saying?
Are they going to pivot here?"

00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:13.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was kind of
holding my breath.

00:08:13.426 --> 00:08:15.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I was not necessaril
the most optimistic

00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:17.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they were going to change
but I was hopeful

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:20.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
that something like this
would be a shock to the system

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:23.236
And I remember we opened back up
in Congress,

00:08:23.236 --> 00:08:27.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was the most
raw and emotional moment

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:28.674 line:92%
in my government career, Seth,

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
just that moment
when we opened back up.

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:33.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember the Republicans
started speaking,

00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:36.315 size:84% position:42%
some of my colleagues,
and they just literally

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:38.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
picked up
the same piece of paper,

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
the same speech
that they were going to give

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:43.322 size:88% position:44%
just hours before as if
this had never happened.

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:46.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's
when my heart sunk again.

00:08:46.893 --> 00:08:49.061 line:92%
Just what is it gonna take

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:51.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, what is it gonna tak
for us to move forward?

00:08:51.097 --> 00:08:54.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what you said
about the coronavirus,

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:55.067 size:75% position:38% line:92%
we lost a colleague.

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:59.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
We lost a young Republican
member of Congress

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:01.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
who died
because of the coronavirus

00:09:01.007 --> 00:09:03.976
We had a moment of silence
for him on the House floor

00:09:03.976 --> 00:09:07.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if my Republican colleague
truly believed

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:10.216
what they said about him
that day and honored him,

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:12.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
they would do so
by wearing a mask.

00:09:12.818 --> 00:09:16.155
Again, these are just connected.
We are just seeing how

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:17.390 line:92%
they are not changing their ways

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:21.060
after these massive change
and these massive shocks,

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.795 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and it is so disturbing.

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:24.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think it's very easy
for those of us

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
who mostly see you
and your colleagues on C-SPA

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:30.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
to forget
that you also have families,

00:09:30.336 --> 00:09:31.103 size:84% position:42% line:92%
you also have children.

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:33.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you have
two young children,

00:09:33.072 --> 00:09:34.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
